      "min_content_run": 3,
      "note": "Counts main-thread turns since the last Agent/Task dispatch, and fires only if the window ALSO contains a contiguous run of at least 3 CONTENT turns -- alm#833's own unit and its own dollar-derived break-even, not a constant chosen here. Both halves matter: a long gap during orchestration or narration is not a missed handoff, because those turns structurally cannot move. This is a PROXY over a proxy. alm#833 validated its three-class labelling at 94.8% agreement against 120 hand labels and states plainly that it is biased; a fired flag here means 'this looks like work that could have moved', never 'this should have moved' -- dependency ordering between turns is not visible to it (alm#833 found 20 of 25 sampled spans dependency-ordered). In a window the gap is also a FLOOR on one side and a CEILING on the other: a dispatch older than the window is invisible, so `turns_since_dispatch` is reported as 'at least' the window's own length when no dispatch is seen.",
