      "measure": 11,
      "measure_of": "safely-mergeable consecutive single-Bash-call pairs in the window",
      "note": "Counts CONSECUTIVE pairs of single-Bash-call turns that alm#831's dependency proxy finds SAFE to merge: no token in B's command came from A's recorded output, and B is not a near-duplicate retry of A (jaccard < 0.60). A merge removes one turn, and one turn is one cache-replay tax payment -- that is the whole reason the count is interesting. It is a PROXY and alm#831 reports its own false-positive and false-negative rates against hand labels; read the count through those, not instead of them. It is also a FLOOR in a window: a pair whose first half sits before the window's start is not visible here, and `window.spans_are_local` tells you the window has a start.",
